Parent: #276

Implement Prompt 13 only: target-owned 500-work operational proof.

Scope:
- reverify prerequisites and exact target/donor identities;
- select governed seed and canonical durable parent;
- perform fail-closed no-write preflight;
- dispatch and independently verify an explicitly gated target-owned exact-inventory run when prerequisites are satisfied;
- prove continuation and durable recovery where possible;
- retain machine-readable `500-work-target-revalidation.json` and a human-readable observation report.

Boundaries: no Hugging Face/Zenodo publication, public metadata changes, donor presentation changes, secrets, or unrelated feature work. Any prerequisite or execution gap remains an explicit blocker.

Parent: #276

Implement Prompt 14 only: evidence-based historical coverage and 33,693-candidate reconciliation.

Scope:
- verify 68 batches, candidate/reviewed/acquired/normalised/stored/published populations from primary artifacts;
- produce deterministic machine and human coverage reports plus mismatch ledger;
- enumerate unsupported candidate-as-acquired claims for Prompt 17 correction;
- add fail-closed validators and tests preventing semantic count collapse.

Boundaries: no changes to existing closeout/evaluator documents, Hub cards, Zenodo metadata, publication, donor archival presentation, or the independent legislation product.

Implement Prompt 17 as a narrowly scoped evidence-governance correction.

Scope:
- inventory legislation consolidation evidence and public completion claims;
- add a typed canonical evidence index with active/superseded/invalidated/historical/incomplete/externally-blocked classifications;
- preserve historical records byte-for-byte and add superseding records;
- separate code migration, operational-state migration, corpus custody/recoverability, and publication-identity migration;
- prevent active evaluators from accepting invalidated evidence;
- produce `evidence-index.json` and `corrected-closeout.md`.

Boundaries: no Prompt 18 release-note changes, Prompt 15 Hub metadata changes, Prompt 19 donor presentation changes, external publication, DOI minting, or historical evidence rewrite.

Implement Prompt 18: correct the formal cutover release cycle-1 recovery-run provenance through a transparent dated addendum, preserving the original historical wording and run records.

Scope:
- independently verify both cycle chains from primary GitHub evidence;
- add a governed local addendum and machine-readable remote-readback receipt;
- apply the authorised release-body correction and verify it remotely;
- do not change state, workflows, Hub/Zenodo metadata, general closeout documents, donor state, or `edithatogo/legislation`.

Conductor track: `conductor/tracks/cutover_release_provenance_correction_20260902/`.
